# Semantic-judge verdict cache: a per-machine cost optimization, NOT a trust
# record. A committed cache can be forged to mark a bad translation "clean" and
# skip the judge, so it must never be committed. (locks.json in the same dir IS
# meant to be committed — the record of human-approved locks — so ignore only
# the cache file, not the .shipi18n/ directory.)
.shipi18n/semantic-cache.json
